{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.85,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["T4", "R3", "T8"],
      "pins": ["T4.1", "R3.2", "T8.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0024", "+3V3", "/NET0044"],
      "observed": "In the KiCad netlist, T4 is connected only by pin 2 to GND and pin 3 to /NET0044; T4 pin 1 (base) does not appear on any net. R3 pin 1 is on NET0024, but R3 pin 2 is on +3V3, so R3 is acting as a pull-up on the IO0/float net rather than as the base drive resistor for T4.",
      "expected": "T4 is intended to be the BT3904 pre-driver for the main pump MOSFET T8, so its base must be driven from the corresponding control/interlock net. The SPICE deck shows R3 between NET0024 and /NET0073, which is consistent with a base resistor to T4, and the specification states that the main pump gate is pre-driven via a BT3904 level shifter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"T4\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"T4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"E\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R3\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R3\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R3 NET0024 /NET0073 4.7k"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "gate driven through R1 (100 Ω) from the ESP32 pin, pre-driven via T1 (BT3904 NPN level shifter)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The main pump gate pre-driver/interlock is inoperative. T8's gate is left driven only by IO10 through R15 and pulled up by R9; if IO10 is not actively driven low, the main pump can remain enabled, and the intended hardware cutoff/level-shift behavior is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, isolation, I2C, and TMC2209 connectivity otherwise match the intended r2 architecture, but T4's base is open in the netlist, breaking the intended main-pump pre-driver/interlock path."
}

